  "model_slug": "epiv-6-way",
  "short_model": "Belimo 6-way EPIV",
  "aliases": [
    "EP..R-R6+BAC",
    "6-way pressure-independent valve"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Actuator / valve (6-way pressure-independent change-over valve)",
  "applies_to": "Belimo 6-way EPIV EP..R-R6+BAC on Modbus RTU, per 6-way EPIV Modbus Register en-gb 2024-01 (general notes dated 16.12.2019).",
  "summary": "Belimo's 6-way EPIV serves two circuits (sequence 1 and sequence 2) through one valve and controls the flow in each with its own flow sensor. Over Modbus RTU one setpoint register covers both sequences (0-33 % and 67-100 %, with a closed dead band in between); the map also gives position, flow in three units, the active sequence, Vmax per sequence and fault flags.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 10,
    "baud": 38400,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 2,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "1-based",
    "note": "Belimo prints each register twice: 'No.' counts from 1 and 'Address' from 0, and the documented value here is the No. column. Register No. 1 (setpoint) is wire address 0. Every value sits in one flat table, so holding-register reads (FC 3) and writes (FC 6/16) reach everything; FC 4 input-register reads of the same addresses also work."
  },
  "default_word_order": "CDAB",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Modbus Register - 6-way EPIV",
    "doc_number": "6-way EPIV Modbus Register en-gb 2024-01",
    "revision_date": "2024-01",
    "url": "https://www.belimo.com/mam/general-documents/system_integration/Modbus/belimo_Modbus-Register_6way-EPIV_en-gb.pdf",
    "pages": "General notes p. 2; register overview p. 3; register description pp. 4-6"
  },
  "notes": [
    "32-bit values occupy two registers with the low word first (Belimo's worked example: No. 10 = 14551, No. 11 = 19 gives 19 x 65536 + 14551 = 1,259,735), so they are UINT32 with CDAB word order. Write a 32-bit pair with one FC 16 request covering only those two registers.",
    "Belimo states all values are unsigned 16-bit integers; unsupported registers read 65535. Writable registers from No. 101 up are persistent.",
    "The factory Modbus address of this valve is 10, not 1.",
    "The flow-setpoint pair (No. 14/15) is read-only in the description table even though the overview's access column is hard to read; it is listed as read-only.",
    "This edition has no bus watchdog or bus-fail registers, and the bus terminator must be fitted externally (120 ohm).",
    "Registers 3, 108-110 are unused and not listed."
  ],
